      "date": "2026-11-14 07:48:56.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(2 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nThe fix looks correct: the new bounds check runs under lod_getref(), so ltd_tgts_size and the bitmap can't be resized underneath it. It needs a refresh to add the Fixes: tag. While at it, consider adding a sanity test, since `lfs setstripe -o` passes the OST indices to the MDS unchecked (only lmm_stripe_offset is checked in lod_verify_v1v3()). For example, `lfs setstripe -o 0,1000 $DIR/$tfile` on a small test filesystem should now fail with EINVAL and not LBUG the MDS.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
