        "subject": "LU-21208 lod: bounds-check OST index in lod_alloc_ost_list",
        "message": "LU-21208 lod: bounds-check OST index in lod_alloc_ost_list\n\nlod_alloc_ost_list() validates each OST index from a user-defined\nspecific-OST striping with test_bit(ost_idx, m->lod_ost_bitmap),\nbut never checks ost_idx against m->lod_ost_descs.ltd_tgts_size\nfirst. lod_ost_bitmap is grown lazily by ltd_add_tgt() only up to\nthe highest index actually registered, so an out-of-range ost_idx\n(e.g. a stale or mistyped OST index never added to the target\ntable) makes test_bit() read past the end of the allocated bitmap.\nThe resulting garbage bit can appear set, letting the bad index\nthrough to LTD_TGT(), which returns NULL, and that NULL reaches\nlod_statfs_and_check()'s LASSERT(tgt), crashing the MDS with an\nLBUG instead of returning -EINVAL.\n\nAdd the same ltd_tgts_size bounds check already used by\nvalidate_lod_and_idx() in lod_lov.c before calling test_bit() in\nlod_alloc_ost_list().\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5\nChange-Id: I788ff956f874d7dbcdf2f03f5ebba5fc7eb64328\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70835\nReviewed-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Keguang Xu <kxu@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
